Viewing applied Fiscal Models

On the left-hand side of the fiscal models form, you can see the list of available fiscal models in the database. You can also filter at the top to just the Applied Models to only view the current model applied to the case. If you click on the name of a model, you can see the notes about it on the right to see what it is calculating and the rates for taxes or royalties. 

To apply a new fiscal model

1.Put a check-mark next to the model name - it will most likely be the name of the state or province that the well is in. You can only apply one model from each tree structure. The default trees are a Country & Miscellaneous. The miscellaneous tree is where you could add other non-tax cash formula models that you may need to apply.

2.To edit the default values for the model, go to the Forms flyout and click on the Fiscal Terms forms that you'll see at the bottom of the standard Forms list. Any forms listed here will contain the inputs for the fiscal model that you have applied, such as tax rates or anything that might affect the fiscal regime that you selected. 

3.Double-click on the form to view it and adjust the rates. 
 
